-- K10
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a tie of paragraph (2)` `descendant of a sibling`)
-- K11
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a tie of paragraph (2)` `sibling of a parent`)
-- K12-K16: first cousin, uncle's spouse, mother-in-law, brother-in-law: no tie constructor exists for a tie the text omits; the caller says `no tie` (SCOPE)
-- K16
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a body of persons held by the person or by a relative of the person` (25%))
-- K17
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` (`a body of persons held by the person or by a relative of the person` (24.99%))
-- K18 (20% plus 5% with a relative), K19 (two companies held by one person), K20 (indirect holding): the encoding takes the largest fraction as the whole (assumption A3), no entry point to add holdings inside the tie (SCOPE)
-- K21
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` `a trustee as paragraph (4) describes`
-- K22
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative` `a trustee as paragraph (4) describes`
-- K23
#ASSERT NOT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` (`a body of persons held by the person or by a relative of the person` (30%))
-- K24
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` (`a tie of paragraph (1)` `sibling`)
-- K25
#ASSERT `s 88 — the tie makes a relative, for the exemption in section 97` (`a tie of paragraph (2)` `descendant of a sibling`)

