-- the sale fixture of section 88
GIVEN cons IS A NUMBER
      rem  IS A NUMBER
      imps IS A LIST OF `An improvement of the asset`
      hold IS A NUMBER
      isale IS A NUMBER
      ibuy  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A sale of an asset`
`ind sale:` cons `, remaining price` rem `, improvements` imps `, holding expenses` hold `, index at sale` isale `, index at purchase` ibuy MEANS
    `A sale of an asset` WITH
        `consideration`                      IS cons
        `remaining original price`           IS rem
        `improvements`                       IS imps
        `remaining holding expenses`         IS hold
        `index on the sale day`              IS isale
        `index on the purchase day`          IS ibuy
        `index on 31 December 1993`          IS 100
        `purchase day`                       IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `sale day`                           IS YMD 2020 1 1

GIVEN e IS A NUMBER
      i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An improvement of the asset`
`an improvement of` e `finished at index` i MEANS
    `An improvement of the asset` WITH
        `remaining expense of the improvement` IS e
        `index on the day the improvement was finished` IS i

`ind lost reading` MEANS `the half of the holding expenses that is left out is lost from the adjusted price`

-- CG01
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital gain` (`ind sale:` 1500000 `, remaining price` 1000000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 100 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 500000
-- CG01
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital loss` (`ind sale:` 1500000 `, remaining price` 1000000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 100 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 0
-- CG02
#ASSERT `s 88 — the capital gain` (`ind sale:` 900000 `, remaining price` 1000000 `, improvements` (EMPTY) `, holding expenses` 0 `, index at sale` 100 `, index at purchase` 100) EQUALS 0
-- CG02
